<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤμιλλα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a game</i> in which nuts, etc.,
			were thrown into a ring (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὤμιλλαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					9.102
				</span></i>
			): hence metaph. of a <i>party, circle,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὤ. ἀριστήσομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					250
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσειμ᾽ εἰς ὤ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					288
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
